{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>[Or it was known</b> that it was known], <b>and its owner did not guard it.</b> This is surely an a fortiori argument: if when he guarded it and it went out and caused damage he is liable for not having guarded it, how much more so. And what does the verse mean by <b>and its owner did not guard it</b>? Rather, the verse added another guarding requirement on top of his [ordinary] guarding, and that is muzzling. Another interpretation: to teach you that one does not punish based on inference alone. Another interpretation: <b>and its owner did not guard it</b> — to include an unpaid bailee."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The lemma reflects the sequence in Exod. 21:36; the first bracketed words (אשר נודע) appear to be part of the verse citation preceding the main lemma 'ולא ישמרנו'. 'נשיכה' (muzzling/biting) likely refers to guarding the animal's mouth; rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:40.798207302Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}